From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:50:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] ci: build and publish patched backend images on hosted
 runners

Build the optimized amd64 backend and source-package authority helper on a
standard Ubuntu runner, with the Wasm runtime gate enabled. Reclaim unused
host SDKs, cap the builder at 12 GiB without additional swap, use two Cargo
jobs, and serialize backend LLVM optimization. Report disk availability
throughout compilation so runner capacity is measured rather than assumed.

Reuse build layers through a GHCR registry cache and persist a bounded
2 GiB sccache mount through Actions cache. Skip cargo-chef cooking on these
ephemeral builders: registry layers do not restore the Cargo target mount,
and cooking the default dependency graph duplicates work before the final
feature-unified build. Persistent local builds retain the existing default.

Check capabilities, structured-error imports, runtime tools and SQLite
startup before pushing an image tagged with the source revision. Publish
the immutable pull digest in the job summary for downstream consumers.

Validated with actionlint and ShellCheck, Dockerfile and workflow shell
syntax checks, and review of the build/cache boundaries. The first hosted
run will establish whether the cold build fits runner disk and time limits.
